{
  "version": "web_agent_v1",
  "description": "Web-agent eval cases. Single-turn cases have no chat_id; multi-turn flows share a chat_id (UUID) across cases and order with `sequence`. The runner sets that chat_id as the LangGraph thread_id, so the production checkpointer threads history naturally.",
  "notes": [
    "All cases currently point at one staging agent (106f41ee-e09f-4536-8e38-c8178145429a). Once a second 'shopify_only' eval agent exists, repoint product-003 to it to test KB-less product routing.",
    "Multi-turn flows: turns sharing a chat_id run serially in `sequence` order. The runner scopes the thread_id with the eval_run_id so re-running this dataset doesn't inherit yesterday's history.",
    "Setup turns are marked `score_judges: false` so they build conversation context without dragging down judge averages — only the final turn of each multi-turn flow is scored."
  ],
  "cases": [
